RAWMSESSION.CONF(5)

# NAME

rawmsession.conf - rawm desktop-session lifecycle configuration

# DESCRIPTION

*rawmsession*(1) uses libconfig syntax. Configuration describes one primary
process and the complete set of long-lived sidecars whose lifecycle belongs to
the rawm desktop session.

The built-in defaults start *rawm*(1) as the primary, with *picom*(1) as the
supervised sidecar. In normal mode configuration is layered in
this order:

. built-in defaults
. _${SYSCONFDIR}/rawm/rawmsession.conf_ (normally _/etc/rawm/rawmsession.conf_)
. _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rawm/rawmsession.conf_, when *XDG_CONFIG_HOME* is absolute;
  otherwise _$HOME/.config/rawm/rawmsession.conf_

A later *primary* setting replaces the earlier primary command. A later
*sidecars* setting replaces the complete sidecar list.

With *rawmsession -c path*, the system and user files are skipped: built-in
defaults are followed by exactly _path_. A missing explicitly selected file is
an error. Missing normal system or user files are not errors.

Unknown settings, wrong types, empty commands, invalid sidecar names, and
duplicate sidecar names are fatal configuration errors. Use *rawmsession -C*
to validate the effective configuration without starting the window manager or
any sidecar.

Libconfig *@include* directives are supported. Relative include paths are
resolved relative to the directory of the configuration file being loaded.

# PRIMARY

*primary* = (string, ...)
	Required non-empty argument vector defining the session-primary process.
	Element zero names the executable. The stock value is:

```
primary = ("rawm");
```

The primary defines session lifetime. rawmsession never respawns it after it
exits. This is intentional: an ordinary rawm SIGHUP performs an in-place WM
restart without changing the process identity seen by rawmsession.

# SIDECARS

*sidecars* is a list of groups. Presence of the setting replaces the complete
sidecar set inherited from an earlier configuration layer. An empty list is
valid and means rawmsession supervises no sidecars.

```
sidecars = (
  { name = "compositor"; command = ("picom"); }
);
```

Each sidecar accepts exactly these settings:

*name* = string
	Required unique lifecycle identifier. Names contain one or more characters
	from *A-Z*, *a-z*, *0-9*, period, underscore, or hyphen. The name is used
	for diagnostics and has no process-discovery or security meaning.

*command* = (string, ...)
	Required non-empty argument vector. Element zero names the executable;
	remaining elements are passed unchanged. rawmsession uses *execvp*(3)
	directly and never invokes an implicit shell.

A sidecar is semantically long-lived. Any exit while the session remains alive
is unexpected, including status zero. The command must therefore remain in the
foreground; do not use daemon/background options such as *picom -b*.
rawmsession restarts an exited sidecar after 250 ms.
After five restart attempts within a ten-second window, that sidecar is
disabled for the remainder of the current session instance. SIGHUP of
rawmsession starts a fresh session instance and therefore resets the restart
budget.

There is deliberately no per-sidecar *restart* switch. If a process is not
supposed to remain alive, it is not a sidecar and does not belong in this file.

# OWNERSHIP

The stock file contains only session infrastructure:

```
primary = ("rawm");
sidecars = (
  { name = "compositor"; command = ("picom"); }
);
```

Do not add ordinary applications merely to make them start with X. Doing so
would declare that rawmsession should restart them whenever they exit.
Likewise, Pinentry belongs to gpg-agent, and authentication tools such as
rawlock are invoked when needed rather than supervised continuously.

If a compositor is intentionally owned by another service manager, remove that
sidecar from this list rather than running two supervisors for the same process.
Status collection is internal to rawm and is not a rawmsession sidecar.

# EXAMPLES

Run Picom with an explicit profile:

```
sidecars = (
  {
    name = "compositor";
    command = ("picom", "--config", "/home/alice/.config/picom/picom.conf");
  }
);
```

Run rawm without supervised sidecars:

```
sidecars = ();
```

# SEE ALSO

*rawmsession*(1), *rawm*(1), *picom*(1)
